  "question": {
    "text": "For sodium light, the two yellow lines occur at <math><msub><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> wavelengths. If the mean of these two is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6000</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>∘</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>∘</mo></mover></math>, then the approximate energy difference between the two levels corresponding to <math><msub><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is"
  },
